  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall begin before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.\r\rReason: This is required by Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).",
    "The rating level of the noise determined by the cumulative sound emissions of the plant to which this permission relates shall be at least 5dBA lower than the existing background noise level at any given time of operation. The noise levels shall be measured or predicted 1m externally to any window at the nearest residential facade and the measurements and assessment shall be made according to BS 4142:2014.\r\rReason: To ensure satisfactory living conditions for neighbouring occupiers, in accordance with policy D14 of the London Plan 2021 policy DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "The site and building works required to implement the development shall be only carried out between the hours of 08.00 and 18.00 Mondays to Fridays and between 08.00 and 13.00 on Saturdays and not at all on Bank Holidays and Sundays\r\rReason: To safeguard the amenity of the neighbours by minimising impacts of the development that would otherwise give rise to nuisance.",
    "The store shall be only open between the hours of 07.00 and 23.00hrs and no other time, as indicated in the acoustic report submitted.\r\rReason: To safeguard the amenity of the neighbours by minimising impacts of noise that would otherwise give rise to nuisance.",
    "Prior to any deliveries taking place, an Operational Management Plan shall have been submitted to and approved by the LPA. The plan must include:\r- expected number of vehicle movements \r- location of parking bays\r- maximum noise levels\r\rThe use shall only be carried on in accordance with the Operational Management Plan. \r\rReason: To safeguard the amenity of the neighbours by minimising impacts of vehicle movements and noise that would otherwise give rise to nuisance in accordance with Policy DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy."
  ],
